## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic SwiftUI parity of the web `DashboardSettingsModal` as **11 files** under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/DashboardSettingsModal.*`, committed as `d0a8b9317` along with the log.

**Surface (faithful to the web source):** all four sections — Identity (name field + 16-emoji 8-column icon grid), Vehicle Filter (scope picker with "All Vehicles" sentinel), Auto-Refresh (6 cadences), Display (two switches) — over a pinned header + footer. The presentational web modal is widened with **every required state**: loading / empty (dashboard not found) / error (retry) / populated, plus stale + offline freshness on the fleet vehicle list — never a blank box. `handleSave`'s rename/icon/update deltas are ported exactly.

**Architecture:** binds through the P1/S8 source seam (no HTTP in the view), P1/S9 generated design tokens, the P1/S10 per-surface i18n table (36 keys; web `dashSettings.*`/`common.*` names preserved), P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, and the P4-core shared `TSButton`. No edits to `project.yml`/lint configs/shared catalog (parallel-unsafe, outside scope).

